land: boot stage marks written straight to dip

arm_init, bsd_init and IOFindBSDRoot each record a LANDK2 block in the
marks ring of dip.  land_mark() never uses the console, so it still reports progress
when the early print path is what is broken.  No site before STARTUP: ml_io_map is not
a serviceable call that early, and a mark must not become the fault it reports.
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
index bb2a2bf..544182e 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -473,9 +473,14 @@ bsd_rooted_ramdisk(void)
  * of the tro_ucred field so that the uthread structure can be
  * used like any other.
  */
+/* land: stage marks (pexpert/arm/land_sdhci.c) go straight to dip: before
+ * percpu_init() the console path can fault, and a fault there prints nothing. */
+extern void land_mark(const char *tag);
+
 void
 bsd_init(void)
 {
+	land_mark("bsdinit");
 	struct uthread *ut;
 	vnode_t init_rootvnode = NULLVP;
 	struct proc_ro_data kernproc_ro_data = {
